  "verbalization": "Secosubamolide appears to have a shared relationship with Fibrinogen beta chain through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Secosubamolide to Elongation factor 1-alpha 2, which is then targeted by (1S)-2-Cyclohexen-1-ol, a compound that ultimately targets Fibrinogen beta chain. The second pathway connects Secosubamolide to the sodium/bile acid cotransporter, which is targeted by 2,2-Dimethyl-3,4-dihydrochromene-4,6-diol, which also targets Fibrinogen beta chain. The third pathway links Secosubamolide to Methyl 2-acetyl-3,5-dihydroxyphenylacetate, which targets Fibrinogen beta chain. These pathways suggest that Secosubamolide may act through different molecular intermediates to influence Fibrinogen beta chain, potentially through a common mechanism involving the regulation of protein synthesis or function. The evidence supports a plausible but not definitively established relationship, with the exact mechanism remaining to be elucidated.",
